config VIDEO_HISTB_VENC
	tristate "HiSilicon HiSTB H.264 encoder driver"
	depends on ARCH_HISI || COMPILE_TEST
	depends on V4L_MEM2MEM_DRIVERS
	depends on VIDEO_DEV
	select VIDEOBUF2_DMA_CONTIG
	select VIDEOBUF2_VMALLOC
	select V4L2_MEM2MEM_DEV
	help
	  Support for the VEDU video encoder family on HiSilicon HiSTB
	  set-top-box SoCs. Both generations are stateful encoders: a raw
	  picture goes in and H.264 network abstraction layer data comes out,
	  with the parameter sets and the slice headers written by the driver.

	  The v2 VEDU of hi3716cv200 and hi3798mv100 -- the part the vendor
	  calls V2R8, built through its venc_v1.0 layer -- is programmed by
	  register writes and a 64-byte packet ring, and codes IDR pictures. The
	  v5 V500 of hi3798mv200h (HiVEDUV500R001, the venc_v2.0 layer) takes a
	  command image in DMA memory, owns a memory-management unit and codes P
	  pictures too.

	  The backend suffix is the hardware generation the block belongs to,
	  taken the same way in both video blocks: v2 is this family's VEDU V2R8
	  and VDH V2/V3, v5 is VEDU V500 and VDH V5R6. It is not the vendor's
	  venc_vX.Y layer number, which counts the other way round.

	  To compile this driver as a module, choose M here: the module will be
	  called histb-venc.
